  "body": "## What happens\n\nThe shipped `Sinker EDM (ISO)` post refuses Sinker Side Burn.\nThis prevents the catalog case in #2872 from posting both required operations.\n\nThe post gives this message:\n\n`a Sinker Side Burn moves the electrode sideways - this post writes a straight burn down Z only`\n\n## Cause\n\nAt upstream/main `58cb641c`, `assets/posts/sinker-iso.cps` supports straight Z burns only.\n`startPreamble()` rejects a Side Burn operation.\n`onLinear()` also rejects feed moves with X or Y travel.\n\nThe existing test `a_sinker_side_burn_is_refused_by_name` pins this limit.\nIt checks the message and confirms that the post emits no `M101` burn code.\n\n## Required result\n\nAdd supported Side Burn posting with explicit machine dialect data.\nKeep named refusals for unsupported machine data and unsafe moves.\nTest the lateral direction, amount, units, condition, and electrode reference.\nRecord and inspect the resulting NC program.\n\nDone means: A valid Side Burn posts its stated lateral burn safely.\nThe straight Sinker Burn still posts correctly.\nThe #2872 case can post both burns through the shipped sinker post.\n\nFound while working on #2872. Catalog umbrella: #2392.\nEffort: high. This change affects posted G-code and uses the safety floor.\n",
